# The modules that the kernel of hd-kernel-server keeps of the config of Debian; make
# localmodconfig turns off every other module. What the config of Debian builds into the kernel
# stays. A line is one of:
#
#   <dir>/    every module of the directory <dir> of the kernel tree and of those below it
#   !<dir>/   none of the directory <dir> and of those below it, of a directory kept above
#   <module>  the module of that name, as lsmod prints it; the build stops when the kernel has no
#             module of that name, as a module or built in
#   <a>|<b>   the names of one module in different kernels, as in trixie and unstable; the
#             build stops when the kernel has none of them
#
# Everything but the drivers stays: file systems, network protocols and netfilter, crypto, and
# kvm. Of the drivers only those of the hardware of the servers (technogea and migrate, from the
# survey of lsmod of 2026-11-01) stay, and the drivers of software that are not hardware.

# Everything but the drivers, and not the protocols of hardware that a server has not.
arch/
block/
crypto/
fs/
kernel/
lib/
mm/
net/
!net/6lowpan/
!net/atm/
!net/bluetooth/
!net/can/
!net/dsa/
!net/ieee802154/
!net/mac80211/
!net/mac802154/
!net/nfc/
!net/phonet/
!net/qrtr/
!net/rfkill/
!net/wireless/
security/
virt/

# Not the users of RDMA, which needs InfiniBand: RDS, SMC, NFS and SMB over RDMA, and 9p, of
# which only the transports over TCP and virtio stay.
!fs/smb/smbdirect/
!net/9p/
!net/rds/
!net/smc/
!net/sunrpc/xprtrdma/
9pnet_fd
9pnet_virtio

# Not the network protocols that the kernel loads when any user opens a socket of them, which
# HyprDebian does not use: SCTP and TIPC. Not the file systems that are rarely used and have had
# holes: cramfs, freevxfs, jffs2 and hfs; hfsplus and udf stay, for disks of macOS and for DVDs.
!net/sctp/
!net/tipc/
!fs/cramfs/
!fs/freevxfs/
